learnings:
  - A Stop hook must honour stop_hook_active or any violation unfixable within a turn loops forever
  - Hook classification must skip generated state at any depth (*/.paradigm/*), not just the repo root
  - npm ignores a newly added override when a lockfile exists; prefer an in-range or major upgrade over overrides plus hand-edited locks
  - Declaring a workspace build tool once at the root lets npm hoist it instead of nesting a copy per package
  - A fresh worktree build exposes packages missing from the build chain that stale dist folders hide
